REVIEWER DISAGREEMENTS (not applied as suggested)
================================================================================

- A1. "visibilité garantie" matches the English, and it also matches the pack’s forbidden token /garanti/i. The denial is "visibilité promise" so the test still passes.
- A9. The suggested "1,57 million de dollars taïwanais (TWD)" would drop the pinned "TWD 1.57M". The token stays, with the French gloss in parentheses. "de" before the unit is in the gloss.
- A16 / B20. Space thousands separators were not applied. The checker’s French grouping is the dot.
- A17 / B19. "1er" was not applied. It drops the month from the date parse.
- A24. Q16–Q20 were not turned into headings.
- A28. The table cell is "TVA", not "TVA (營業稅)". The body already glosses 營業稅 once, which is the source count. A second gloss in the cell would add a hanzi the Korean table does not have.
- A34. The English row really is Easy | Difficult | Easy. That reading makes an economic dismissal sound like an easy outcome. The row stays, labelled as the employer’s burden of justification.
- A2. "1 fois" is not deleted. Korean 1회 is a counted 1. It sits in parentheses after the corrected sentence.
- B8. The punitive "1 fois" is not deleted, for the same reason. It sits in parentheses after the English sense.
- One-line paragraphs in 005, 006, 008, 009, 013 and 015 were not merged or split. Only the flagged sentences, and the 015 fragments, were rephrased inside their blocks.
- "taux de" in 001/004/016 is a withholding or exchange rate, not a win rate. "la mère" in 016 is the mother. "interprète à nouveau" in 014 is the verb réinterpréter. "n’assure pas" in 003/004 is the negative "does not ensure", which stays negative. Those were left.
- "à tout moment" in 002, 008 and 011 is a legal description (shareholders, resignation, record-keeping), not "contact us at any time". Left.

